## 📋 Spec Analysis

- **Feature name:** SmartQC — Test Case Generator Full Pipeline
- **Feature type:** Combined (Claude Project platform; generates test cases for Web/API/Mobile features)
- **Actors:** QC Engineer, Tester, QA Manager
- **Main flows:**
  1. User uploads/pastes a `.md` spec → Skill analyzes spec → Generates test cases → Generates report template
  2. Skill auto-detects feature type, platforms, actors, business rules
  3. Skill applies security masking if sensitive data is found in spec
  4. Skill outputs versioned artifacts with version header
  5. If generation is incomplete, skill stops cleanly and provides resume instruction
- **Business rules:**
  - Output must include both artifacts (test cases + report template) in one run
  - TC IDs follow `TC-[MODULE]-[NUM]` convention
  - Priority auto-assigned per defined rules
  - Sensitive data must be masked before output; warning displayed only if detected
  - Retry up to 3 attempts on failure; partial output flagged clearly
  - Version bumps: same spec = patch, updated spec = minor, rewrite = major
  - Language output matches spec language
- **Ambiguities:**
  - No explicit timeout value for "no response" in Claude Project context (Section 8 says 30s but Claude Project does not expose raw API timeout to users)
  - "Rollback" (Section 9) implies persistent file storage, but Claude Project has no native file versioning
  - "Stored as separate files pushed to GitHub" (Section 9) — no GitHub integration is described elsewhere
  - Section 8 retry logic — unclear whether this is handled by the skill prompt or an external orchestration layer

